{"school":{"dbn":"27Q105","name":"P.S. 105 The Bay School","boro":"Queens","district":"27","district_label":"District 27","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"K-8","grades":"K to 8","status":"open","enrollment":600,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"420 BEACH 51 STREET, QUEENS, NY 11691","phone":"718-634-3382","website":"www.psms105qbayschool.com","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/72570","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"Our vision is to promote a nurturing environment that enhances teacher practice and raise the level of student achievement and overall success. PS/MS 105 most recently had a 100% graduation rate for our past 8th grade class. Our school offers students the opportunity to be involved in sports, chess, music, art, and STEAM activities in science classes. The middle school science classes incorporate CS4ALL curriculum. Some classes are also offered before and after school (CHAMPS Program). Our 8th grade students were able to take extensive regents preparation course in mathematics to have the ability to take the Algebra regents examination. The technology is improving each year with the addition of more laptops and Promethean Boards in every classroom. The auditorium has been redesigned by the Bette Midler Foundation. There are a series of after school clubs involved with CMS that are offered throughout the school year and students are given the chance to be a part of school plays, dance, and even cook.","start_time":"08:15am","end_time":"02:15pm","languages":null,"subway":"A to Beach 44th St","bus":"Q22, Q52-SBS, QM17","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Far Rockaway","latitude":40.595678,"longitude":-73.781259,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.848],"st":["ok"],"n":[352.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.888